tes_grand_prix_-_infringement_-_car_5_-_pu_elements.pdf","publicado":"23.10.26 20:52","piloto":"Gabriel Bortoleto","codigo":"BOR","sesion":null,"hecho":"The following Power Unit elements have been used: 4th Energy Store (ES) 4th Control Electronics Unit (PU-CE)","decision":"Drop of 20 grid positions for the next Race in which the driver participates.","decision_es":"Pierde 20 puestos en la grilla","tipo":"grilla","proxima_carrera":true},{"id":"b86e7bf66a42","titulo":"Doc 14 - Infringement - Car 43 - PU Element","url":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_united_states_grand_prix_-_infringement_-_car_43_-_pu_element.pdf","publicado":"23.10.26 20:44","piloto":"Franco Colapinto","codigo":"COL","sesion":null,"hecho":"The following Power Unit elements has been used: 4th Control Electronics Unit (PU-CE)","decision":"Drop of 10 grid positions for the next Race in which the driver participates.","decision_es":"Pierde 10 puestos en la grilla","tipo":"grilla","proxima_carrera":true}],"mejoras":{"titulo":"Doc 11 - Car Presentation Submissions","url":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_united_states_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf","publicado":"23.10.26 17:00","equipos":[{"equipo":"McLaren Mastercard F1 Team","mejoras":[{"componente":"Front Corner","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"Revised Front Corner and Furniture The front corner scoop and furniture have been revised in conjunction with the front suspension fairings aiming at improved flow conditioning."},{"componente":"Rear Corner","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"Updated Rear Corner Furniture The rear corner furniture has been revised to achieve an improvement in flow conditioning as well as increased local load."},{"componente":"Diffuser","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"New diffuser geometry The diffuser geometry has been modified aiming at an improvement of flow conditioning and local load across the speed range."}],"leido":true},{"equipo":"Mercedes-AMG PETRONAS F1 Team","mejoras":[],"leido":true},{"equipo":"Oracle Red Bull Racing","mejoras":[{"componente":"Front Wing","motivo":"Rendimiento: más carga en la zona","detalle":"Additional vane on the endplate foot plate Taking the recently introduced front wing geometry, an option to operate with the tyre temperature turning vane has been added for evaluation, offering a tyre surface temperature measurement as well as more local load with similar flow stability."},{"componente":"Front Corner","motivo":"Fiabilidad","detalle":"Elastomeric gaitor profile revision The periphery of the gaitor has been revised to reduce the likelihood of tearing the elastomeric material during running by reducing the strain in the regions of highest deflection when steering lock is applied."}],"leido":true},{"equipo":"SCUDERIA FERRARI HP","mejoras":[],"leido":false},{"equipo":"Williams","mejoras":[],"leido":true},{"equipo":"Visa Cash App Racing Bulls","mejoras":[{"componente":"Front Wing","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"New front wing endplate The front wing endplate plays an important role in managing the flow around the front tyres. These updates further improve the management of the flow field downstream."},{"componente":"Rear Wing","motivo":"Rendimiento: más carga en la zona","detalle":"New flap elements The camber and chord of the rear wing flap elements has been modified to clean up the local flow and allow the wing to generate more load."},{"componente":"Floor Body","motivo":"Rendimiento: más carga en la zona","detalle":"Multiple changes including leading edge devices, board and floor edge A combination of developments across a number of key floor components which improves the overall flow management around the floor. This translates into an efficient downforce increase."},{"componente":"Coke/Engine Cover","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"Reprofiled shoulder and undercut Working in combination with the updates made to the floor, the changes to the engine cover help manage the flow as it passes around the side of the car and towards the rear."}],"leido":true},{"equipo":"Aston Martin Aramco F1 Team","mejoras":[],"leido":true},{"equipo":"TGR HAAS F1 TEAM","mejoras":[],"leido":true},{"equipo":"Audi Revolut F1 Team","mejoras":[{"componente":"Front Corner","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"New front brake duct The revised front brake duct provides updated cooling characteristics together with associated aerodynamic performance, complementing the latest development steps introduced."},{"componente":"Front Floor","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"New Floor Board The updated floorboard geometry is intended to improve local flow conditioning and support the overall aerodynamic performance of the floor assembly."},{"componente":"Mirror Stay","motivo":"Rendimiento: mejor flujo de aire","detalle":"New Mirror Stay The updated mirror stay geometry complements the revised front corner configuration and supports the overall aerodynamic performance of the car package introduced lately."}],"leido":true},{"equipo":"BWT Alpine F1 Team","mejoras":[{"componente":"Floor Corner","motivo":"Rendimiento: más carga en la zona","detalle":"Redesigned rear floor corner The rear floor corner has been redesigned to improve the local flowfield interaction with the rear corner while also increasing local load."},{"componente":"Rear Wing","motivo":"Rendimiento: más carga en la zona","detalle":"Reprofiled rear wing flap The second and third element flap of the rear wing have been redesigned to improve rear wing flow quality and overall load delivery."}],"leido":true},{"equipo":"Cadillac","mejoras":[],"leido":false}]}},"actualizado":"2026-10-23T20:15:21+00:00","fuentes":{"Jolpica":{"ok":true},"OpenF1":{"ok":true},"FIA":{"ok":true}}}